<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>Self-study quiz.</strong> This quiz is for your own review — answers are not recorded. You’ll get instant feedback on each question.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="quiz"><div class="quiz__top-bar"><div class="quiz__score-tracker" style="display:none;"></div><button class="quiz__start-over" type="button" style="display:none;">Start Over</button></div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q1a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">1</span> According to this lesson, the subject matter of music is</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1a" id="q1a">
        <label for="q1a">feeling: the structures and patterns of feeling, such as tension and release, buildup and resolution.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1b" id="q1b">
        <label for="q1b">the names of specific emotions only.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1c" id="q1c">
        <label for="q1c">historical events.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1d" id="q1d">
        <label for="q1d">the lives of composers.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. A painting of a sad woman shows you sadness; music enacts the structure of sadness in sound.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The lesson argues that music bypasses representation and presents patterns of feeling directly.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q2c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">2</span> What is the difference between consonance and dissonance?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2a" id="q2a">
        <label for="q2a">There is no difference.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2b" id="q2b">
        <label for="q2b">Consonance is for singers and dissonance is for pianos.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2c" id="q2c">
        <label for="q2c">Consonance is a pleasing combination of simultaneous tones; dissonance is a tense, unresolved combination.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2d" id="q2d">
        <label for="q2d">Consonance is loud and dissonance is quiet.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Dissonance creates tension that the music may later resolve; that tension and release is part of musical feeling.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Consonance sounds stable and pleasing; dissonance sounds tense and unresolved.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q3d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">3</span> In Beethoven's Fifth Symphony, the four-note opening is best called</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3a" id="q3a">
        <label for="q3a">a harmony.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3b" id="q3b">
        <label for="q3b">a dynamic.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3c" id="q3c">
        <label for="q3c">a counterpoint.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3d" id="q3d">
        <label for="q3d">a motive: the smallest self-contained unit of a theme.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Beethoven transforms, inverts, extends, and develops this motive obsessively across the first movement.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The short-short-short-long figure is the smallest self-contained unit that the movement is built from. That is a motive.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q4a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">4</span> What claim do formalists make about music?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4a" id="q4a">
        <label for="q4a">Its value lies entirely in its internal structure, so external references are unnecessary.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4b" id="q4b">
        <label for="q4b">Its value lies in the emotions it refers to beyond itself.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4c" id="q4c">
        <label for="q4c">It must always be paired with lyrics.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4d" id="q4d">
        <label for="q4d">It has no value.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. A formalist hears the Fifth as a masterpiece of structural logic.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Formalists focus on form: the relationships among tones, rhythms, and harmonies, not on external meanings.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q5b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">5</span> What claim do expressionists make about music?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5a" id="q5a">
        <label for="q5a">Only the structure of music matters.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5b" id="q5b">
        <label for="q5b">Music refers to emotions and experiences beyond itself, as a minor key connects to our experience of sadness.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5c" id="q5c">
        <label for="q5c">Music must be about politics.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5d" id="q5d">
        <label for="q5d">Music has no connection to emotion.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. An expressionist hears the Fifth as an embodiment of struggle and triumph. The lesson says both views are right, and neither is complete without the other.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Expressionists emphasize what music expresses. A minor key sounds sad because it connects to our experience of sadness.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q6c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">6</span> How does Billie Holiday's performance of "Strange Fruit" make a devastating subject harder to ignore?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6a" id="q6a">
        <label for="q6a">She changes the words to a happier story.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6b" id="q6b">
        <label for="q6b">The song has no lyrics.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6c" id="q6c">
        <label for="q6c">She sings softly and conversationally, with long pauses between lines, which sets the beauty of her voice against the horror of the content.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6d" id="q6d">
        <label for="q6d">She sings as loudly as possible.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The artistic form does not soften the subject matter; it makes it harder to look away.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Think about contrast. A quiet, beautiful voice describing something terrible forces the listener to attend to the words.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q7b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">7</span> What is a raga in Indian classical music?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7a" id="q7a">
        <label for="q7a">A kind of drum.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7b" id="q7b">
        <label for="q7b">A framework of notes, patterns, and emotional associations that the performer uses as the basis for improvisation.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7c" id="q7c">
        <label for="q7c">A Western melody played slowly.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7d" id="q7d">
        <label for="q7d">A fixed written composition that cannot change.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The raga provides the rules, and the performer's spontaneous choices within those rules create the content.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">A raga is not a single melody. It is a set of rules and associations that the performer improvises within.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q8b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">8</span> A piece that opens with a theme, moves to a contrasting section, and then returns to the opening theme is in</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8a" id="q8a">
        <label for="q8a">call-and-response form.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8b" id="q8b">
        <label for="q8b">ternary (ABA) form.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8c" id="q8c">
        <label for="q8c">no form at all.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8d" id="q8d">
        <label for="q8d">binary (AB) form.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The return in ABA gives a feeling of homecoming after the contrast.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">A return to the opening after a contrast makes an A-B-A pattern, called ternary form.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q9a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">9</span> Bach's Prelude from his first cello suite is built from</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9a" id="q9a">
        <label for="q9a">a repeating pattern of broken chords, so a single instrument suggests several voices at once.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9b" id="q9b">
        <label for="q9b">a single sustained note.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9c" id="q9c">
        <label for="q9c">a spoken text.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9d" id="q9d">
        <label for="q9d">a loud percussion pattern.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The pattern outlines changing harmonies, and the listener hears a slow harmonic journey inside the quick motion.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The piece is famous for a pattern that outlines chords one note at a time on a single cello.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q10d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">10</span> On the first pass of the three-pass method of listening, you should</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10a" id="q10a">
        <label for="q10a">analyze every note.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10b" id="q10b">
        <label for="q10b">read the lyrics only.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10c" id="q10c">
        <label for="q10c">listen to a different piece.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10d" id="q10d">
        <label for="q10d">follow the overall shape of the music: where it starts, builds, relaxes, and ends.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The second pass is for elements such as tempo, rhythm, melody, and dynamics, and the third is for expression and the choices that produce it.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The first pass is for the big picture. Details come on later passes.</div>
  </div>
</div>

